      "doc_type": "data_definition",
      "title": "Institutional and Program Outcomes",
      "url": "https://my.cgu.edu/institutional-effectiveness/institutional-and-program-outcomes/",
      "summary": "The Institutional and Program Outcomes page at Claremont Graduate University outlines the learning objectives and expected skills for various academic programs. It details institutional learning outcomes for all graduates, such as knowledge within their disciplines, research and inquiry skills, effective communication, transdisciplinary methods, and career-specific skills. The page breaks down specific competencies and learning outcomes for different departments and degrees, including arts and humanities, management, health sciences, and more. The document serves as a comprehensive guide for students to understand the core competencies and learning achievements associated with their programs.",
      "stored": false,
      "fetched_at": "2026-06-01T18:39:37.555474+05:30"
    },
    {
      "doc_type": "data_dictionary",
      "year": 2026,
      "title": "Institutional Research",
      "url": "https://www.cgu.edu/about/administration/academic-affairs/office-of-institutional-effectiveness/institutional-research/",
      "summary": "The Institutional Research office at Claremont Graduate University supports the university by providing accurate, timely, and reliable information related to academic and operational activities. It responds to requests for statistical information, gathers and analyzes data on faculty, staff, student populations, programs, and resources. The office ensures accurate data collection through adherence to the AIR Code of Ethics. Available statistics include enrollment, admissions, program fees, and demographic information on students and faculty.",
      "stored": false,
      "fetched_at": "2026-06-01T18:39:32.630464+05:30"
    },
    {
      "doc_type": "data_dictionary",
      "title": "Institutional Research",
      "url": "https://cgu.edu/about/institutional-research",
      "summary": "The Institutional Research office at Claremont Graduate University is part of the Office of Institutional Effectiveness. It provides accurate, timely, and reliable information related to the academic and operational activities of the university, serving CGU personnel, management, the state and federal governments, accreditation agencies, local and national surveys, and the general public. The office is responsible for gathering, analyzing, and reporting information on faculty, staff, student population, programs, and resources. It also helps with research methodology, evaluation, and data analysis. The office adheres to the Code of Ethics of the Association for Institutional Research to ensure accurate data collection.",
      "stored": false,
