      "summary": "The Institutional Research office at Claremont Graduate University provides accurate, timely, and reliable information on the university's academic and operational activities. It serves requests from CGU personnel, management, and external entities including state and federal governments, local and national surveys, and accreditation agencies. The office offers statistics and reports on topics such as enrollment, admissions, faculty and staff demographics, academic programs, and degrees conferred. It adheres to the Code of Ethics by the Association for Institutional Research (AIR).",
